# The changelog entries below the "Releasing Matomo X.Y.Z" line are a verbatim
# transcription of upstream's release notes, scraped from matomo.org. Their
# wording is upstream's, not the maintainer's, and lintian's misspelling list
# regularly flags it (a doubled word in 5.5.0, "Allow to" in 5.7.0, ...).
#
# One override for the tag rather than one per occurrence: lintian only inspects the
# *latest* changelog entry, so an override quoting a given sentence stops matching
# at the next release and turns into a mismatched-override warning on every later
# package. The narrow form would cost one override per release and one warning per
# release after it. No context at all, so it cannot drift: lintian matches an
# override without context against every instance of the tag.
matomo-vanilla: spelling-error-in-changelog

# Override the jquery-mousewheel embedded-library warning in Matomo 5.7.0
matomo-vanilla: embedded-javascript-library please use libjs-jquery-mousewheel [usr/share/matomo/node_modules/jquery-mousewheel/jquery.mousewheel.min.js]
